{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1496707-magical-identity","id":1496707,"title":"Magical Identity","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-11-10T09:53:44-08:00","id":1496707,"title":"Magical Identity","content":"Inspired by the conversation on yantras and dedicated magical tools (here: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1496401-dedicated-tools-as-yantras\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...ols-as-yantras</a> )<br /> <br /> I want to get my head around how identity work in Mage.<br /> <br /> When casting magic the Shadow name is the most obvious way your identity affects a spell, but that is a subset of the Persona yantra bonuses, which include the related Cabal theme, and the less obviously connection resonantly charged mana.<br /> <br /> The other parts of your identity are the engrained Path tools, and the more changeable Order tools.<br /> <br /> And lastly SoS talks about using any item touched by your Signature Nimbus as a magical tool (with the same +1 as a path or order tool), removing the signature Nimbus in the process. The soulstone being Imprinted with your signature Nimbus is a more extreme version of this, giving a +2 bonus on spell casting (though is even more than that, given how other mages can use your soul stone aswell).<br /> <br /> It seems like this could be simplified by looking at them all together as one type of identity related idea...<br /> <br /> Also does the Mana infused with resonance make slightly more sense in the context of using your nimbus and how shadow name affects your long term Nimbuses effects?<br /> <br /> I think there is more to be said about Long term Nimbuses and faults, when it comes to magical identity (especially when the lesser Tulpa of a Rapt mage appears to be like a (significantly) stronger version of the long term Nimbus, and the greater Tulpa appears to be a supernal being - possibly one created as a pure expression of your magical self - which in the rare case of Walkers the conscious self can merge with.<br /> <br /> ** Somehow i missed the bit on SoS where Investiture can be used as a +1/+2/+3 yantra bonus based on your status/mystery cult initiation merits. Which i think is the best Nameless Orders have to offer compared to Order tools...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 01-19-2023, 06:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-10T10:20:07-08:00","id":1496709,"title":"","content":"While ultimately more focused on Wisdom than Magical Identity, I <i>start</i> the entire essay on the subject of identity as semiotics which is Supernally Powerful, so the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/887107-understand-wisdom?p=895967#post895967\">Understand Wisdom</a> essay from ages ago might be helpful.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Anyways, is there a specific question, or is just going for a broad look/explanation about magical identity?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 11-10-2022, 02:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-10T11:46:41-08:00","id":1496721,"title":"","content":"There is only one specific question in there, it is mostly an attempt to get some ideas about magical identity in one place... But more that i am open to a discussion.<br /> <br /> The question being about how resonance and signature Nimbus might be related, especially when it comes to resonant mana being usable as a persona yantra bonus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-15T15:35:06-08:00","id":1497231,"title":"","content":"Ok, identity as a path to ascension.<br /> <br /> So i am going to take some theoretical leaps here. Supposing that a Greater Tulpa is the Supernal reflection of your magical identity. Perhaps a twisted version of the ideal, but nevertheless a true Supernal Being which is able to interact with the Fallen through its essence lining up with your magical identity. <br /> <br /> In a sense it is you (or rather your magical identity) but the Supernal version - like how a Daimon in the Oneirous is an Astral version of you... But also not exactly.<br /> <br /> Drawing back, for non-rapt characters the Supernal interacts with the Fallen through your long term Nimbus (and the more Gnosis you have the more interactions it has). It has not coalessed into a Supernal Being, but it is still your magical identity as expressed through rhe supernal. <br /> <br /> So Ascension can be seen as purifying yourself, to become that Supernal entity, that entity which is your magical identity. Maybe the way you express your shadow name doesn't perfectly align with the Supernal version of yourself, but as your shadow name grows it becomes stronger and shapes your magical identity. Maybe by studying your Nimbus and integrating it into your shadow name you can increase the potency of both - possibly unlocking more Gnosis... (And arcane beats). <br /> <br /> The implications are clear, the Rapt would be broken entities dissociated from their magical identity somehow, their likelihood of ascending much lower. <br /> <br /> And Ascension would be deeply personal..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-19T03:29:05-08:00","id":1500715,"title":"","content":"Another thought on this, most from reading up on the Rapt and Long term Nimbuses, it feels like a long term Nimbus can be like a proto-verge. It is explicitly usable as a summoning circle for greater Tulpas, which dies with the Rapt mage.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of spreading your magical identity around or using it to create a verge (just requires your actual soul, not just a soul stone...).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}